1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,206
Nine twelve.

2
00:00:01,256 --> 00:00:04,233
The nine o'clock patient isn't coming.

3
00:00:04,283 --> 00:00:09,650
Her deposit is held on PayPal, and
only the owner's tap can keep it.

4
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:15,298
I run qnowa: deposit booking
for clinics in Latin America.

5
00:00:15,348 --> 00:00:19,650
The first thing owners ask:
can it touch my money?

6
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:22,096
Deposits stop no-shows.

7
00:00:22,146 --> 00:00:26,749
But every day someone decides:
keep, release or give back.

8
00:00:26,799 --> 00:00:31,403
Our agent can hold money on
its own: a hold moves nothing.

9
00:00:31,453 --> 00:00:33,650
To move it, it can only ask.

10
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:36,602
Eleven forty-eight at night.

11
00:00:36,652 --> 00:00:38,869
Lucía books Monday at nine.

12
00:00:38,919 --> 00:00:43,992
The agent creates a PayPal order
that only holds ten dollars.

13
00:00:44,042 --> 00:00:49,535
She approves it, a signed notice
tells the agent, and it confirms.

14
00:00:49,585 --> 00:00:51,047
Held, not charged.

15
00:00:51,097 --> 00:00:53,650
The owner's phone stayed quiet.

16
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:55,935
Nine twelve again.

17
00:00:55,985 --> 00:00:59,866
The agent can't take the deposit; it asks.

18
00:00:59,916 --> 00:01:07,354
The phone shows what gets signed, not what
the AI wrote: keep up to ten dollars,

19
00:01:07,404 --> 00:01:09,132
this booking, once.

20
00:01:09,182 --> 00:01:15,310
One tap signs it, and the approval
id becomes PayPal's request id.

21
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:17,650
One tap, one PayPal call.

22
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:19,391
Mid-morning.

23
00:01:19,441 --> 00:01:24,335
Lucía writes that her son
was in the emergency room.

24
00:01:24,385 --> 00:01:28,329
A kind assistant would refund on the spot.

25
00:01:28,379 --> 00:01:30,230
Ours can't; it asks.

26
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:33,368
And sometimes the owner says yes.

27
00:01:33,418 --> 00:01:35,650
Her money, her decision.

28
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:43,727
Someone pretends to be the owner: nothing
reaches her phone, nothing reaches PayPal.

29
00:01:43,777 --> 00:01:48,267
The agent reuses an approval:
rejected as a replay,

30
00:01:48,317 --> 00:01:51,650
and written down like everything else.

31
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:53,360
One thirty.

32
00:01:53,410 --> 00:01:59,417
Sofía cancels, in Spanish, and
the agent answers in Spanish.

33
00:01:59,467 --> 00:02:05,070
We only held her money, so
this is a void, not a refund:

34
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:09,511
it moves zero dollars
and releases the hold.

35
00:02:09,561 --> 00:02:13,650
Still the owner's call, so still one tap.

36
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:15,478
Closing time.

37
00:02:15,528 --> 00:02:16,517
Three taps.

38
00:02:16,567 --> 00:02:22,942
On its own, the agent made five
PayPal calls and moved zero dollars.

39
00:02:22,992 --> 00:02:29,650
Every attempt, even the refused one,
sits in a ledger anyone can check.

40
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:32,211
Not only a simulation.

41
00:02:32,261 --> 00:02:37,650
Capture, void and refund ran
against the real PayPal sandbox.

42
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:40,817
Can it touch my money?

43
00:02:40,867 --> 00:02:42,567
It can hold it.

44
00:02:42,617 --> 00:02:45,017
Only you can move it.

45
00:02:45,067 --> 00:02:46,650
Ask First Pay.
